Linux kernel
============

There are several guides for kernel developers and users. These guides can
be rendered in a number of formats, like HTML and PDF. Please read
Documentation/admin-guide/README.rst first.

In order to build the documentation, use ``make htmldocs`` or
``make pdfdocs``.  The formatted documentation can also be read online at:

    https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/

There are various text files in the Documentation/ subdirectory,
several of them using the Restructured Text markup notation.
See Documentation/00-INDEX for a list of what is contained in each file.

Please read the Documentation/process/changes.rst file, as it contains the
requirements for building and running the kernel, and information about
the problems which may result by upgrading your kernel.


MID1020L source audit
=====================

This repository is currently a MediaTek Android kernel 4.19.191 source tree;
it is not the tablet's confirmed 4.9.190 stock source. The working branch
``porting/mid1020l-audit-scaffold`` contains the source-research report and
reproducible, pinned source-fetch script. No stock configuration or device
partitions have been modified.

See ``SOURCE_AUDIT.md`` for candidate-by-candidate findings and known gaps.
Run ``bash tools/mid1020l-fetch-sources.sh`` to fetch the pinned, relevant
external reference trees under ``sources/``. The fetch script refuses to
overwrite existing destination directories. Its output is for offline
inspection only; it is not a validated kernel port or flashable image.

Current assessment: Flitsmeister's public 4.19.191 tree provides exact
``tb8768p1_64_bsp`` platform/DTS and the exact US105 GSLX68X touchscreen
profile. It is the strongest public hardware reference found, but it does
not establish 4.9.190 API/BSP compatibility. Its HX8279 panel files are
for other named panel variants; the exact ``us105_fx_hx8279_boe_wuxga_ips_101``
initialization source has not been located. Do not reuse a related panel's
sequence or wiring as a substitute.
